* ICPS2023_5 BSIMSOI v4.4 (ngspice LEVEL=58) bridge candidate.
*
* Generated by tools/fit_b4soi_bridge.py.  ADJUSTED BRIDGE CANDIDATE:
* it changes the stage-1 reference card and must not be selected as the
* nominal model without re-running the IV/AC-charge/dynamic regressions.
*
* Data: PDK_minimalFabSOICMOS.pdf p.7 (Level 1 table) and the digitized
* p.10-11 curves (459 samples) in ../fit/.  Bulk-DIBL/mobility priors come
* from the same-process-line card models/legacy_MF_CMOS20240109_bulk3.inc.
*
* KNOWN CONFLICTS, retained rather than hidden:
*  - the p.7 PMOS threshold row (-0.71 V) disagrees with the p.10-11 PMOS
*    transfer curves (turn-on near |VGS| = 0.45 V), so VTH0 is a BOUNDED FIT;
*  - the p.7 single subthreshold-slope number is not simultaneously attainable
*    for both digitized curves of a device; the fit uses the p.7 value as a
*    deadband target and lands inside the measured spread.
* See audit/b4soi_bridge_fit.md and audit/b4soi_bridge_candidate_verification.md.
*
* SOIMOD=2 (ideal-FD) is deliberate, for self-consistency with this card's own
* NCH=1e15 premise (W_d,max = 863 nm >> TSI = 95 nm, so no neutral body region
* can exist) and NOT as a claim about the measured device. SOIMOD=0 imposes a
* partially-depleted premise the film contradicts, which is also a numerical
* pathology (T7 120 ns: >1e7 steps at SOIMOD=0 vs 6.1e3 at SOIMOD=2). Unified
* mode 1 is stable only for some parameter sets. The real device's depletion
* mode remains a TEG question (AGENTS.md 1.2 and 6).
*
* Parameter provenance for nch (NMOS):
*   fixed   LEVEL      ngspice BSIMSOI v4.4 selector (BSIM4SOI). Not BSIM4/LEVEL=54.
*   fixed   SOIMOD     Ideal-FD equations, chosen for electrostatic self-consistency with this card's own AGENTS.md 4.1 premise, NOT as a claim about the measured device. NCH=1e15 gives W_d,max=863 nm >> TSI=95 nm, so no neutral body region can exist and the SOIMOD=0 partially-depleted premise is contradicted; that mismatch is also a numerical pathology (T7 120 ns: >1e7 steps at SOIMOD=0 vs 6.1e3 at SOIMOD=2). Unified mode 1 is not a safe substitute: it is stable for some parameter sets and stiff for others (7.8e3 vs >1e7 steps), whereas mode 2 was stable for every set measured. Mode 2 and mode 1 give identical DC here (transfer 0.1931 vs 0.1932 decades). The real device's depletion mode remains a TEG question (AGENTS.md 1.2, 6).
*   fixed   MOBMOD     Unchanged from the stage-1 reference.
*   fixed   CAPMOD     Unchanged from the stage-1 reference.
*   fixed   TNOM       PDK characterisation temperature (p.7, Ta=25 C).
*   fixed   TOX        PDK p.4/p.7 measured gate oxide 15 nm.
*   fixed   TOXM       Equals TOX; no oxide-thickness scaling is characterised.
*   fixed   TSI        AIST-SOI-CMOS.xs cross-section prior 95 nm (Level 2).
*   fixed   TBOX       AIST-SOI-CMOS.xs cross-section prior 400 nm (Level 2).
*   fixed   XJ         Unmeasured placeholder, XJ <= TSI; not copied from the bulk card.
*   fixed   NGATE      TiN metal gate, no polysilicon depletion; midgap work function (AGENTS.md 2.3).
*   fixed   NCH        AGENTS.md 4.1: removes the bulk-BSIM3 NCH=1.7e17 residue; W_d,max >> TSI.
*   fixed   K2         No body-bias sweep constrains the second-order term (AGENTS.md 2.3).
*   fitted  VTH0       Start = PDK p.7 table value; bounded fit per user decision 2026-10-16 (digitized transfer curves vs p.7 row conflict).
*   derived K1         K1 = sqrt(2*q*eps_Si*NCH)/Cox from the same NCH=1.0e15 channel doping.
*   fitted  NFACTOR    Anchored to the PDK p.7 measured subthreshold slope (71 mV/dec).
*   prior   VOFF       Same-line bulk-BSIM3 surrogate subthreshold offset.
*   fitted  U0         Effective low-field mobility; bulk prior 670 cm^2/Vs.
*   prior   UA         Same-line bulk-BSIM3 vertical-field mobility degradation.
*   prior   UB         Same-line bulk-BSIM3 vertical-field mobility degradation.
*   prior   UC         Same-line bulk-BSIM3 lateral-field mobility degradation.
*   prior   VSAT       Same-line bulk-BSIM3 saturation velocity; +/-30% surrogate window.
*   fitted  RDSW       Source/drain access resistance; bounded to the physical contact range.
*   prior   A0         Same-line bulk-BSIM3 bulk-charge/DIBL coefficient; surrogate window.
*   prior   AGS        Same-line bulk-BSIM3 gate-bias dependence of A0.
*   prior   KETA       Same-line bulk-BSIM3 body-bias DIBL coefficient; small physical term.
*   prior   PCLM       Same-line bulk-BSIM3 channel-length modulation; surrogate window.
*   prior   PDIBLC2    Same-line bulk-BSIM3 DIBL term (AGENTS.md 4.1).
*   fixed   CGSO/CGDO  PDK p.9 measured overlap 5 fF/um (AGENTS.md 2.4)
